            <ArticleTitle>Photonic Nanostructures Patterned by Thermal Nanoimprint Directly into Organo-Metal Halide Perovskites.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1002/adma.201605003</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Photonic nanostructures are created in organo-metal halide perovskites by thermal nanoimprint lithography at a temperature of 100 °C. The imprinted layers are significantly smoothened compared to the initially rough, polycrystalline layers and the impact of surface defects is substantially mitigated upon imprint. As a case study, 2D photonic crystals are shown to afford lasing with ultralow lasing thresholds at room temperature.</AbstractText>
